<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27200" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lūna</span></b> , ae, f.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of
				Etruria</i>, now <i>Luni</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 8, § 50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 39,
				21, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">43,
			11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 30, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			482</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lūnensis</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lūniensis</span></b> ,
			e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Luna</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caseus Luniensis, remarkable for its size,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 42, 97, § 241</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 30</span></i>
			<i>in lemm.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmor,</span>”
				<i>the modern marble of Carrara</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 6, 7, § 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					36, 18, 29, § 135</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ara,</span>”
				<i>an altar of marble of Luna</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 50</span></i>
			. —<i>Plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lūnenses</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Luna</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 5,
				4, § 14</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
